{{Bagua}} '''Xun''' (巽) is one of the {{ill|Bagua|ja|八卦|12=draft|12=draft}}. Its trigram form is {{resize|125%|'''☴'''}} with the first {{ill|Yao (lines)|ja|爻|12=draft|12=draft}} being Yin (⚋) and the second and third Yao being Yang (⚊). It is also one of the {{ill|Sixty-Four Hexagrams|ja|六十四卦|12=draft|12=draft}}, known as {{ill|Xun (Bagua)|ja|巽|lt=巽為風|12=draft|12=draft}}, consisting of Xun below and Xun above.
== Trigram Symbolism == Xun symbolizes {{ill|wind|ja|風|12=draft|12=draft}} (also associated with {{ill|wood|ja|木|12=draft|12=draft}}), entry, {{ill|chickens|ja|ニワトリ|12=draft|12=draft}}, the thighs, the eldest daughter (a woman of {{ill|marriageable age|ja|結婚適齢期|12=draft|12=draft}}), {{ill|marriage proposals|ja|縁談|12=draft|12=draft}}, anything long, {{ill|blood vessels|ja|血管|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|hair|ja|毛髪|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|small intestine|ja|小腸|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|large intestine|ja|大腸|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|bronchi|ja|気管支|12=draft|12=draft}}, submersion, and the {{ill|respiratory system|ja|呼吸器|12=draft|12=draft}}. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|12=draft|12=draft}}, it represents the {{ill|southeast|ja|東南|12=draft|12=draft}}, specifically the area between {{ill|Chen (Earthly Branch)|ja|辰|1=Dragon (zodiac)|lt=Dragon (辰)|12=draft|12=draft}} and {{ill|Si (Earthly Branch)|ja|巳|1=Snake (zodiac)|lt=Snake (巳)|12=draft|12=draft}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|12=draft|12=draft}} system, Xun is associated with {{ill|Xin (Heavenly Stem)|ja|辛|1=Kanoto (辛)|12=draft|12=draft}}, the Metal element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|12=draft|12=draft}}, and the {{ill|west|ja|西|12=draft|12=draft}} among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|12=draft|12=draft}}.
== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|12=draft|12=draft}}, Xun corresponds to the {{ill|southeast|ja|東南|12=draft|12=draft}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|12=draft|12=draft}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|lt=Kan (☵)|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt=Gen (☶)|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|12=draft|12=draft}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt\=Dui (☱)|lt=Dui (☱)|12=draft|12=draft}}, and {{ill|Qian|ja|乾|1=Qian (Bagua)|lt=Qian|lt=Qian (☰)|12=draft|12=draft}}—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Because it lies between {{ill|Chen (辰)|ja|辰|1=Dragon (zodiac)|lt=Dragon (辰)|12=draft|12=draft}} (*tatsu*) and {{ill|Si (巳)|ja|巳|1=Snake (zodiac)|lt=Snake (巳)|12=draft|12=draft}} (*mi*), Xun is also read as *Tatsumi* (たつみ).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|12=draft|12=draft}}, Xun is the fifth in sequence and is positioned as one of the four corner trigrams, representing {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|12=draft|12=draft}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the emergence of one Yin.
