[[sn:Xun (Bagua)]] [[ja:巽]] [[ja:太極]] [[ja:乾]] [[ja:兌]] [[ja:艮]] [[ja:離]] [[ja:九星]] [[ja:魔方陣]] [[ja:後天定位盤]] [[ja:五行思想]] [[ja:木]] [[ja:火]] [[ja:土]] [[ja:金]] [[ja:水]] [[ja:十干]] [[ja:十二支]] [[ja:八卦]] [[ja:易経]] [[ja:禹]] [[ja:夏王朝]] [[ja:洛水]] [[ja:洛書]] [[ja:河図洛書]] [[ja:陰陽道]] [[ja:方位]] [[ja:運勢]] [[ja:吉凶]] [[ja:一白水星]] [[ja:北]] [[ja:坎]] [[ja:二黒土星]] [[ja:坤]] [[ja:三碧木星]] [[ja:東]] [[ja:震]] [[ja:四緑木星]] [[ja:五黄土星]] [[ja:六白金星]] [[ja:七赤金星]] [[ja:西]] [[ja:八白土星]] [[ja:九紫火星]] [[ja:南]] [[ja:太陽系]] [[ja:相性]] [[ja:吉方位]] [[ja:易]] [[ja:高島易断]] [[ja:風水]] [[ja:気学]] [[ja:陰陽五行説]] [[ja:暦注]] [[en:draft:Xun (Bagua)]] [[en:Xun]] [[sn:Xun]] [[ko:%EC%86%90 (%EA%B4%98)]] [[pt:X%C3%BAn (I Ching)]] [[nl:Wind (trigram)]] [[fr:X%C3%B9n]] [[sn:un]] [[ar:Xun (Bagua)]]
{{DEFAULTSORT:Xun (Bagua)}}

{{Bagua}} '''Xun''' (巽) is one of the {{ill|Bagua|ja|八卦|qq=draft}}. Its trigram form is {{resize|125%|'''☴'''}} with the first {{ill|Yao (lines)|ja|爻|qq=draft}} being Yin (⚋) and the second and third Yao being Yang (⚊). It is also one of the {{ill|Sixty-Four Hexagrams|ja|六十四卦|qq=draft}}, known as {{ill|Xun (Bagua)|ja|巽|lt=巽為風|qq=draft}}, consisting of Xun below and Xun above.
== Trigram Symbolism == Xun symbolizes {{ill|wind|ja|風|qq=draft}} (also associated with {{ill|wood|ja|木|qq=draft}}), entry, {{ill|chickens|ja|ニワトリ|qq=draft}}, the thighs, the eldest daughter (a woman of {{ill|marriageable age|ja|結婚適齢期|qq=draft}}), {{ill|marriage proposals|ja|縁談|qq=draft}}, anything long, {{ill|blood vessels|ja|血管|qq=draft}}, {{ill|hair|ja|毛髪|qq=draft}}, {{ill|small intestine|ja|小腸|qq=draft}}, {{ill|large intestine|ja|大腸|qq=draft}}, {{ill|bronchi|ja|気管支|qq=draft}}, submersion, and the {{ill|respiratory system|ja|呼吸器|qq=draft}}. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft}}, it represents the {{ill|southeast|ja|東南|qq=draft}}, specifically the area between {{ill|Chen (Earthly Branch)|ja|辰|1=Dragon (zodiac)|lt=Dragon (辰)|qq=draft}} and {{ill|Si (Earthly Branch)|ja|巳|1=Snake (zodiac)|lt=Snake (巳)|qq=draft}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|qq=draft}} system, Xun is associated with {{ill|Xin (Heavenly Stem)|ja|辛|1=Kanoto (辛)|qq=draft}}, the Metal element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=draft}}, and the {{ill|west|ja|西|qq=draft}} among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|qq=draft}}.
== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft}}, Xun corresponds to the {{ill|southeast|ja|東南|qq=draft}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|qq=draft}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|lt=Kan (☵)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt=Gen (☶)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt\=Dui (☱)|lt=Dui (☱)|qq=draft}}, and {{ill|Qian|ja|乾|1=Qian (Bagua)|lt=Qian|lt=Qian (☰)|qq=draft}}—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Because it lies between {{ill|Chen (辰)|ja|辰|1=Dragon (zodiac)|lt=Dragon (辰)|qq=draft}} (*tatsu*) and {{ill|Si (巳)|ja|巳|1=Snake (zodiac)|lt=Snake (巳)|qq=draft}} (*mi*), Xun is also read as *Tatsumi* (たつみ).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=draft}}, Xun is the fifth in sequence and is positioned as one of the four corner trigrams, representing {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|qq=draft}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the emergence of one Yin.
