{{Bagua|qq=}} '''Xun''' (巽) is one of the {{ill|Bagua|ja|八卦|qq=draft|qq=}}. Its trigram form is {{resize|125%|'''☴'''|qq=}} with the first {{ill|Yao (lines)|ja|爻|qq=draft|qq=}} being Yin (⚋) and the second and third Yao being Yang (⚊). It is also one of the {{ill|Sixty-Four Hexagrams|ja|六十四卦|qq=draft|qq=}}, known as {{ill|Xun (Bagua)|ja|巽|lt=巽為風|qq=draft|qq=}}, consisting of Xun below and Xun above.
== Trigram Symbolism == Xun symbolizes {{ill|wind|ja|風|qq=draft|qq=}} (also associated with {{ill|wood|ja|木|qq=draft|qq=}}), entry, {{ill|chickens|ja|ニワトリ|qq=draft|qq=}}, the thighs, the eldest daughter (a woman of {{ill|marriageable age|ja|結婚適齢期|qq=draft|qq=}}), {{ill|marriage proposals|ja|縁談|qq=draft|qq=}}, anything long, {{ill|blood vessels|ja|血管|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|hair|ja|毛髪|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|small intestine|ja|小腸|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|large intestine|ja|大腸|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|bronchi|ja|気管支|qq=draft|qq=}}, submersion, and the {{ill|respiratory system|ja|呼吸器|qq=draft|qq=}}. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft|qq=}}, it represents the {{ill|southeast|ja|東南|qq=draft|qq=}}, specifically the area between {{ill|Chen (Earthly Branch)|ja|辰|1=Dragon (zodiac)|lt=Dragon (辰)|qq=draft|qq=}} and {{ill|Si (Earthly Branch)|ja|巳|1=Snake (zodiac)|lt=Snake (巳)|qq=draft|qq=}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|qq=draft|qq=}} system, Xun is associated with {{ill|Xin (Heavenly Stem)|ja|辛|1=Kanoto (辛)|qq=draft|qq=}}, the Metal element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=draft|qq=}}, and the {{ill|west|ja|西|qq=draft|qq=}} among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|qq=draft|qq=}}.
== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=draft|qq=}}, Xun corresponds to the {{ill|southeast|ja|東南|qq=draft|qq=}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|qq=draft|qq=}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|lt=Kan (☵)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt=Gen (☶)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|qq=draft|qq=}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|2=ja|3=兌|4=zh-yue|5=兌卦|6=ko|7=태 (괘)|8=fr|9=Duì|10=nl|11=Meer (trigram)|12=pt|13=Duì (I Ching)|14=zh-min-nan|15=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt\=Dui (☱)|lt=Dui (☱)|qq=draft|qq=}}, and {{ill|Qian|ja|乾|1=Qian (Bagua)|lt=Qian|lt=Qian (☰)|qq=draft|qq=}}—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Because it lies between {{ill|Chen (辰)|ja|辰|1=Dragon (zodiac)|lt=Dragon (辰)|qq=draft|qq=}} (*tatsu*) and {{ill|Si (巳)|ja|巳|1=Snake (zodiac)|lt=Snake (巳)|qq=draft|qq=}} (*mi*), Xun is also read as *Tatsumi* (たつみ).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=draft|qq=}}, Xun is the fifth in sequence and is positioned as one of the four corner trigrams, representing {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|qq=draft|qq=}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the emergence of one Yin.
