ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Because it lies between {{ill|Chen (辰)|ja|辰|1=Dragon (zodiac)|lt=Dragon (辰)|qq=draft|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chen (辰)|13=User:Immanuelle/Dragon (zodiac)|qq=}} (*tatsu*) and {{ill|Si (巳)|ja|巳|1=Snake (zodiac)|lt=Snake (巳)|qq=draft|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Si (巳)|13=User:Immanuelle/Snake (zodiac)|qq=}} (*mi*), Xun is also read as *Tatsumi* (たつみ).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=draft|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|qq=}}, Xun is the fifth in sequence and is positioned as one of the four corner trigrams, representing {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|qq=draft|qq=|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/southwest|qq=}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the emergence of one Yin.
